<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<definitions xmlns="http://www.omg.org/spec/BPMN/20100524/MODEL" xmlns:bpmndi="http://www.omg.org/spec/BPMN/20100524/DI" xmlns:dc="http://www.omg.org/spec/DD/20100524/DC" xmlns:di="http://www.omg.org/spec/DD/20100524/DI" xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance" id="defs_P_18_3" targetNamespace="http://tim-method.example/utility-wam/1.0" exporter="Utility WAM Industry Process Reference" exporterVersion="2026-08-28">
  <process id="P_18_3" name="18.3 Notify the parties the operation affects" isExecutable="false">
    <documentation>All four processes are drawn. The group has two entries because a first notice and a change notice are different acts: 18.3.4 re-issues on the SAME channel to everyone already told, and says what changed rather than repeating the original.

NO LEAD TIME APPEARS IN THIS FILE. Outage notice periods and the terms of a life-support or medical register are tariff, State or contract, and this reference holds none of them - so the timer carries the lead time as an input rather than a number. 49 CFR 192.615(a)(3) is in the file for contrast only: it requires a prompt and effective response to an EMERGENCY, which is what a planned notice is not, and reaching for it as a planned-notice rule is the most likely way to mis-source this group.</documentation>
    <laneSet id="P_18_3_lanes">
      <lane id="l_183_comm" name="Customer communications">
        <flowNodeRef>n_183_start</flowNodeRef>
        <flowNodeRef>n_183_res</flowNodeRef>
        <flowNodeRef>n_183_third</flowNodeRef>
        <flowNodeRef>n_183_gw</flowNodeRef>
        <flowNodeRef>n_183_t</flowNodeRef>
        <flowNodeRef>n_183_send</flowNodeRef>
        <flowNodeRef>n_183_rec</flowNodeRef>
        <flowNodeRef>n_183_del</flowNodeRef>
        <flowNodeRef>n_183_retry</flowNodeRef>
        <flowNodeRef>n_183_esc</flowNodeRef>
        <flowNodeRef>n_183_done</flowNodeRef>
        <flowNodeRef>n_183_chg</flowNodeRef>
        <flowNodeRef>n_183_what</flowNodeRef>
        <flowNodeRef>n_183_reiss</flowNodeRef>
        <flowNodeRef>n_183_moved</flowNodeRef>
        <flowNodeRef>n_183_cend</flowNodeRef>
      </lane>
      <lane id="l_183_cust" name="Critical customer contact">
        <flowNodeRef>n_183_crit</flowNodeRef>
        <flowNodeRef>n_183_creach</flowNodeRef>
        <flowNodeRef>n_183_hold</flowNodeRef>
        <flowNodeRef>n_183_recrit</flowNodeRef>
      </lane>
    </laneSet>
    <startEvent id="n_183_start" name="Confirmed window published"><messageEventDefinition id="n_183_start_md"/></startEvent>
    <serviceTask id="n_183_res" name="Resolve the impact list to notifiable parties (18.3.1)"><documentation>18.3.1. The 18.1.3 impact list is premises and sections; this is people, organisations and the channel each of them is owed.</documentation></serviceTask>
    <userTask id="n_183_third" name="Add attachers, agencies and adjacent operators"><documentation>18.3.1. Third-party attachers are 11.0's counterparties and an adjacent operator is 19.1.3's. Both are notified here and neither is a customer.</documentation></userTask>
    <exclusiveGateway id="n_183_gw" name="Critical or life-support premises in scope"/>
    <userTask id="n_183_crit" name="Contact each critical premise personally (18.3.3)"><documentation>18.3.3. On the register's terms, which belong to the operator or the tariff. An unanswered message is not a confirmation that somebody vulnerable knows.</documentation></userTask>
    <exclusiveGateway id="n_183_creach" name="Customer reached and arranged"/>
    <endEvent id="n_183_hold" name="Hold or replan the outage"><documentation>18.3.3. Back to 18.2.3 for a different window. The outage moves; the customer does not.</documentation></endEvent>
    <startEvent id="n_183_t" name="Notice lead time reached"><documentation>18.3.2. The lead time is an input. This reference states none.</documentation><timerEventDefinition id="n_183_t_td"/></startEvent>
    <sendTask id="n_183_send" name="Send on each party's channel (18.3.2)"><documentation>18.3.2. Statutory, tariff and contractual notices differ by party and by State.</documentation></sendTask>
    <serviceTask id="n_183_rec" name="Record what was sent, to whom and when"><documentation>18.3.2. The record is the only evidence the notice existed, and 18.3.4 needs the channel it went out on.</documentation></serviceTask>
    <exclusiveGateway id="n_183_del" name="Delivered"/>
    <sendTask id="n_183_retry" name="Retry before the window closes"><documentation>18.3.2.</documentation></sendTask>
    <sendTask id="n_183_esc" name="Escalate a party that cannot be reached"><documentation>18.3.2. Escalation is not the same as delivery and the record says which happened.</documentation></sendTask>
    <endEvent id="n_183_done" name="Parties notified"/>
    <startEvent id="n_183_chg" name="Window changed, deferred or cancelled"><messageEventDefinition id="n_183_chg_md"/></startEvent>
    <userTask id="n_183_what" name="Establish what actually changed (18.3.4)"><documentation>18.3.4. Scope, window or cancellation. Re-issuing the original notice with a new date tells nobody what happened.</documentation></userTask>
    <sendTask id="n_183_reiss" name="Re-issue to everyone already notified, same channel"><documentation>18.3.4. Everyone already told, on the channel they were told on - not the channel that is convenient now.</documentation></sendTask>
    <exclusiveGateway id="n_183_moved" name="Window moved"/>
    <sendTask id="n_183_recrit" name="Re-run the critical-premise contact"><documentation>18.3.4. A moved window is a new arrangement for a life-support customer, not an amendment to the old one.</documentation></sendTask>
    <endEvent id="n_183_cend" name="Change communicated"/>
    <sequenceFlow id="f_n_183_start_n_183_res" sourceRef="n_183_start" targetRef="n_183_res" name=""/>
    <sequenceFlow id="f_n_183_res_n_183_third" sourceRef="n_183_res" targetRef="n_183_third" name=""/>
    <sequenceFlow id="f_n_183_third_n_183_gw" sourceRef="n_183_third" targetRef="n_183_gw" name=""/>
    <sequenceFlow id="f_n_183_gw_n_183_crit" sourceRef="n_183_gw" targetRef="n_183_crit" name="critical premises present"><conditionExpression xsi:type="tFormalExpression"><![CDATA[criticalPremises > 0]]></conditionExpression></sequenceFlow>
    <sequenceFlow id="f_n_183_gw_n_183_t" sourceRef="n_183_gw" targetRef="n_183_t" name="none"/>
    <sequenceFlow id="f_n_183_crit_n_183_creach" sourceRef="n_183_crit" targetRef="n_183_creach" name=""/>
    <sequenceFlow id="f_n_183_creach_n_183_hold" sourceRef="n_183_creach" targetRef="n_183_hold" name="not reached"><conditionExpression xsi:type="tFormalExpression"><![CDATA[reached = false]]></conditionExpression></sequenceFlow>
    <sequenceFlow id="f_n_183_creach_n_183_t" sourceRef="n_183_creach" targetRef="n_183_t" name="reached and arranged"/>
    <sequenceFlow id="f_n_183_t_n_183_send" sourceRef="n_183_t" targetRef="n_183_send" name=""/>
    <sequenceFlow id="f_n_183_send_n_183_rec" sourceRef="n_183_send" targetRef="n_183_rec" name=""/>
    <sequenceFlow id="f_n_183_rec_n_183_del" sourceRef="n_183_rec" targetRef="n_183_del" name=""/>
    <sequenceFlow id="f_n_183_del_n_183_retry" sourceRef="n_183_del" targetRef="n_183_retry" name="not delivered"><conditionExpression xsi:type="tFormalExpression"><![CDATA[delivered = false]]></conditionExpression></sequenceFlow>
    <sequenceFlow id="f_n_183_retry_n_183_esc" sourceRef="n_183_retry" targetRef="n_183_esc" name=""/>
    <sequenceFlow id="f_n_183_esc_n_183_done" sourceRef="n_183_esc" targetRef="n_183_done" name=""/>
    <sequenceFlow id="f_n_183_del_n_183_done" sourceRef="n_183_del" targetRef="n_183_done" name="delivered"/>
    <sequenceFlow id="f_n_183_chg_n_183_what" sourceRef="n_183_chg" targetRef="n_183_what" name=""/>
    <sequenceFlow id="f_n_183_what_n_183_reiss" sourceRef="n_183_what" targetRef="n_183_reiss" name=""/>
    <sequenceFlow id="f_n_183_reiss_n_183_moved" sourceRef="n_183_reiss" targetRef="n_183_moved" name=""/>
    <sequenceFlow id="f_n_183_moved_n_183_recrit" sourceRef="n_183_moved" targetRef="n_183_recrit" name="moved"><conditionExpression xsi:type="tFormalExpression"><![CDATA[windowMoved = true]]></conditionExpression></sequenceFlow>
    <sequenceFlow id="f_n_183_recrit_n_183_cend" sourceRef="n_183_recrit" targetRef="n_183_cend" name=""/>
    <sequenceFlow id="f_n_183_moved_n_183_cend" sourceRef="n_183_moved" targetRef="n_183_cend" name="cancelled or scope only"/>
  </process>
